      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193631_77604_26506" xmi:uuid="5663ff22-352c-4e26-9b60-48a9ad666ccf" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454507412593_835555_43416" xmi:uuid="68fdb27e-ae24-40b7-ad64-4c4392a9e6c2" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193631_77604_26506"/>
          <body> the meaning of the relationship. Where applicable, the following class names shall be used: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;'addition': The business object specifies that the Related document provides supplementary or collateral information with regard to the information provided by the Relating document; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'copy': The business object defines a relationship where the Related Document is a copy of the Relating Document; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'derivation': The business object defines a relationship where the Related Document is derived from the Relating Document; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'peer': The business object specifies that the Related document provides required information with regard to that provided by the Relating document. The peer document is essential for a complete understanding; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'reference': The business object defines a relationship where the Related document is referenced from the Relating; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'substitution': The business object defines a relationship where the Related Document replaces the Relating Document; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'translation': The DocumentRelationship specifies that the Related document is generated through a translation process from the Relating document.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>RelationType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193496_562046_25456"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
