        <name>ClassifiedAs</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193038_880755_23447"/>
        <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194497_424181_32172" xmi:uuid="6ff8cf43-0594-424e-8e3e-44a21cd4974f" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
        <upperValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194496_422901_32171" xmi:uuid="bad0bd13-e742-478d-af4f-fa37487b79d6" xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
          <value>*</value>
        </upperValue>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193480_756444_25359"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193697_123255_26973" xmi:uuid="13cde5a1-b12d-4e35-a3b6-3b4853ff02b7" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454511975079_686719_43502" xmi:uuid="b0d47c7b-1008-474e-9a21-1982685c8034" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193697_123255_26973"/>
          <body> the meaning of the relationship. Where applicable, the following class names shall be used: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;'addition': The business object specifies that the Related File provides supplementary or collateral information with regard to the information provided by the Relating File; &lt;example&gt; The recommended practices for this document may be an addition. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'copy': The business object defines a relationship where the Related File is a copy of the Relating File; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;decomposition': The business object defines a relationship where the Related File is one of potentially more sub documents of the Relating File; &lt;example&gt; The decomposition of a document into clauses or into several CAD models is an example for the use of this value. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'derivation': The business object defines a relationship where the Related File is derived from the Relating File; &lt;example&gt; A raster image may be derived from a three-dimensional CAD model. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; A html version may be derived from a text document as an alternative. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'peer': The business object specifies that the Related document provides required information with regard to that provided by the Relating document. The peer document is essential for a complete understanding; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'reference': The business object defines a relationship where the Related document is referenced from the Relating; &lt;example&gt; A hyperlink is an example for a 'reference'. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'sequence': The business object defines a logical sequence where the Related File comes after the Relating File; &lt;example&gt; A sequence of clauses. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'substitution': The business object defines a relationship where the Related File replaces the Relating File; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'translation': The FileRelationship specifies that the Related File is generated through a translation process from the Relating File.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>RelationType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193500_86382_25478"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
