    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583143250_208868_103890" xmi:uuid="e3347e73-44d6-4d44-949b-35ee04363d07" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_290014c_1538398379570_466095_88978" xmi:uuid="0e601f0d-83c9-4d9e-9950-7df54c528cf6" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-Assigned_document_property-described_element"/>
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-Classification_assignment-items"/>
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-External_source_identification-item"/>
        <body>Entities like Description_text_assignment, Classification_assignment, Identification_assignment, etc. have their items property unmapped in the mapping specification since they have to be completed where used.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529584315738_876129_104015" xmi:uuid="105f025e-71bb-4042-9ea0-a2be0846327e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583143250_208868_103890"/>
        <body>A FileLocationIdentification is the identification of the location where a File can be found. &lt;example&gt;For a computer file identified by a filename and directory path, such as 'D:\project1\specification.txt', the ExternalId attribute represents the filename, 'specification.txt' and the SourceId attribute represents the path name, 'D:\project1\'. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>FileLocationIdentification</name>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583197880_435762_103933" xmi:uuid="e4d78239-47f9-4391-897b-c28fec1bd5f5" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529593104406_349428_108497" xmi:uuid="8bfff320-39a1-4adb-88da-21d219a7b9cf" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583197880_435762_103933"/>
          <body>the text that identifies the context in which the ExternalId is specified. &lt;example&gt;For a digital file identified by a filename and directory path, the SourceId is the directory path.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>SourceId</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193306_841204_23948"/>
        <isOrdered>true</isOrdered>
        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583212076_384065_103936"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583237442_697896_103941" xmi:uuid="aefb4774-85bc-4766-a214-6cbef48546cd" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529593192299_101849_108498" xmi:uuid="8e45da98-d671-4300-9113-25085233c659" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1529583237442_697896_103941"/>
          <body>the text that identifies the identification scheme of the SourceId. &lt;example&gt;In the case of files, examples of SourceType are: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;'URL' - for a web page;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'FTP' - for an FTP address; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'ISBN' - for physical documents.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/example&gt; </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>SourceType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193306_841204_23948"/>
