          <body>the identifier of the external item, in its external context. The value of this attribute need not be specified. If the attribute is not specified, then SourceId completely specifies the file location. &lt;example&gt;For a digital file, the file name of a file in the directory where it is located is an example of ExternalId. &lt;/example&gt; &lt;example&gt;For a book, the ExternalId could be the ISBN number. &lt;/example&gt; </body>
